WEBVTT

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:07.650
<b>“What then is time?
If no one asks me, I know what it is. 
If I wish to explain it to him who asks, I do not know. 
- St. Augustine</b>

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:07.580
<i>Today's special report is about the random 
disappearances everyone is talking about.</i>

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.880
<i>People who were just there a moment 
ago, disappearing into thin air!</i>

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.840
<i>Is it terrorism? Human trafficking 
by criminal organizations?</i>

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:17.770
<i>Or perhaps even Desert Syndrome, a strange 
disease where the human body crumbles away</i>

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.590
<i>as if it was made of sand?</i>

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.850
<i>There are all kinds of 
theories as to the cause.</i>

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.890
<i>Does this modern version of 
"spirited away" truly exist? {Like the Miyazaki movie. The JP word is "kamikakushi", which means "hidden by the gods". IE the gods just up and take you away one day randomly.}</i>

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.270
<i>Or is it merely an urban legend?</i>

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.270
<i>You all know the Breakers responsible for
looking into this, Adios and James.</i>

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:37.780
<i>Spirited away? Desert Syndrome?
That's sheer nonsense.</i>

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.860
<i>First, take a look at these statistics.</i>

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.780
<i>These are statistics of the missing people...</i>

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:24.550
Morning!

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:25.510
You look sleepy.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:26.890
Well, yeah...

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.890
<i>I don't mind my school uniform.</i>

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.600
<i>Wearing the same clothes as everyone
else puts me at ease.</i>

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:36.940
<i>I think it's probably an ancient instinct 
to help me hide from predators.</i>

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:41.570
<i>In the distant past,
back when we were still sheep,</i>

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:45.780
<i>I bet the ones who stood out were 
all eaten by tigers and wolves.</i>

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:47.030
Tohru!

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.160
Morning!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:52.250
Morning, Katagiri.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:55.420
Aww, I told you you can call me Kyoka!

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.340
<i>I suppose she would be one of the tigers.</i>

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:00.960
<i>She has no need to hide.</i>

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.720
That smells good! What was your breakfast?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.930
A typical boil-in-the-bag meal.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.600
Hey, you got some on you here.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:10.930
Let's see...

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:18.360
What's that?

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:23.990
- Hey, what is it? An accident?
- No, I think that's a crime scene.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.070
Maybe it's one of those 
spiriting away things.

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.280
No way. That's just a rumor, right?

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:37.580
What's wrong?

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:42.590
No... it's nothing.  I just 
had a bad dream last night.

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:44.670
There, there.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.680
That bastard!

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.720
Why is he holding her—

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:54.140
Lord Kyohma, I'll hold your bag for you.

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:57.350
Tohru!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:06:00.320
You bastard! Get away from there!

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:03.440
Tohru, Kyoka, good morning!

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:04.780
Oh, geez...

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.610
Sorry. I'm gonna go on ahead.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.240
My sister, are you okay?

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.080
Shut up! You stupid big brother!
Why are you getting in my way?

00:06:15.290 --> 00:06:17.120
<i>I'm fine with being a sheep.</i>

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.540
<i>I hope I'm one of the fluffy ones.</i>

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.840
By the way, how is Tanaka doing?

00:06:27.130 --> 00:06:29.220
He's been absent for three days now, right?

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:31.640
Maybe he got spirited away.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:32.600
Serious?

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.020
There was that road closure
on the way here, right?

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:37.850
I caught a glimpse of it.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.270
Morning!

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:42.520
Is that you, Tanaka?

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.530
Hey, you're still alive!

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:51.800
2nd Far East Imperial City
Management District

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.780
6th Far East Imperial City
Management District

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.540
As shown here, the dissolution of the nation 
known as Japan during the 21st century

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:57.600
34th Far East Imperial City
Experimental Development District

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:56.140
5th Gyges Direct
Control District

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.180
17th Far East Imperial City
Management District

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:59.040
coincidenced with the 
rise of megacorporations.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:01.020
40th Far East Imperial City
Experimental Development District

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:02.040
Cottus Special Resource District

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.040
This meant the end of the 
existing national government.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.630
The completion of the KK Matrix 
further accelerated this dissolution.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:13.220
Kazasumi, explain what the KK 
Matrix and its sixth index are.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:14.010
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:14.890 --> 00:07:21.270
The KK Matrix is the basis for the ranking system,
and the sixth index is your genetic potential

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:22.520
for things like muscular 
strength and physical stamina.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:23.940
<i>The ranking system.</i>

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:28.240
<i>It analyzes a human's abilities 
and potential at the genetic level</i>

00:07:26.570 --> 00:07:29.240
17th Far East Imperial 
 City Management District

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:31.780
<i>and assigns each person to the most fitting 
occupation to keep society stable.</i>

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.490
Old Japan Division Of Power Map

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.580
<i>Of course, that's a big fat lie.</i>

00:07:35.330 --> 00:07:38.910
<i>The fact that you have a high rank
just means that your parents are rich.</i>

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:43.210
<i>Since I don't have any parents, I've 
got no chance of going above rank D.</i>

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.090
<i>If I tried to fight against it, 
I'd just stand out in a bad way.</i>

00:07:47.130 --> 00:07:48.840
<i>"The nail that sticks up gets hammered down."</i>

00:07:49.220 --> 00:07:54.050
<i>From what history I've learned, even in the distant past
when the country called Japan still existed,</i>

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:56.680
<i>this was that sort of place.</i>

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:00.350
Do your best!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.480
Do your best!

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:07.860
Tohru!

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.360
Good luck!

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.200
Sure. Though I don't like this class
all that much.

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:15.080
My sister!

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.830
How are you doing?

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.910
It's my stupid big brother again...

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:23.290
Tohru, beat the crap out of this moron.

00:08:23.290 --> 00:08:24.170
The crap?

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:26.460
Well...

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.220
Kyoka, you're in the girls' finals, right?
Good luck to you, too.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:31.630
Yeah! I won't lose.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.640
I hope to have a good match with you.

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.810
The pleasure's all mine.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.110
Four... three... two...

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.820
<i>I guess it's about time?</i>

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.540
<i>Shizune, where did you go?</i>

00:09:02.540 --> 00:09:06.710
<i>We have two players left
in both the boys' and the girls' groups!</i>

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.170
Oh no, I'm still—

00:09:09.550 --> 00:09:12.090
Let's have some fun!

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:17.470
Prepare yourself!

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:24.770
What are you doing?
I would've died if I took that hit just now!

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:28.440
Oh, I'd thought that you'd be able
to easily dodge that, Lady Kyoka.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:31.320
<i>Just what is your problem with me?</i>

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:33.280
<i>I don't have a problem with you.</i>

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:37.870
<i>Do you understand just how much
Lord Kyohma worries about you?</i>

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.790
Um... shouldn't we stop this?

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.870
It's so nice to be young.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:48.590
You're quite different, 
aren't you Tohru Kazasumi?

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.000
This is stupid.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.840
If you're not participating, then shut up.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.850
I'll give you my stupid big brother then!

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:04.560
Stupid? How dare you say that
about Lord Kyohma!

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.690
What a pain!

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:09.560
I don't care.
Just hurry up and take Tohru already!

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:10.940
I-I know that!

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.410
And you should keep
my stupid big brother on a leash!

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:30.170
<i>The girls' match has ended.
The final winner is Kyoka Katagiri.</i>

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.140
<i>Here.</i>

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.560
Ouch...

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:55.530
<i>The boys' match has ended.
The final winner is Kyohma Katagiri.</i>

00:10:57.360 --> 00:10:59.240
Thank you very much.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.200
Don't mess with me like that.

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.190
My stupid big brother really went too far.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:32.980
I'm sorry.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.860
Oh no. It's not a big deal.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:38.070
Tohru, you're too nice.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.610
There's nothing wrong with 
beating my big brother!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:46.410
I do like how you're so modest, Tohru, but...

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.960
You know, Tohru, I think you'd be pretty amazing
if you gave it all you've got.

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.170
No... I don't think that's—

00:11:54.170 --> 00:11:55.960
You could be super-important!

00:11:58.130 --> 00:11:59.550
Like the president!

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.470
The president?

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:03.850
That's so passé.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:07.350
And anyway, all the important 
people do is fight in wars.

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.850
You can end all the wars, then!

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:13.480
How about becoming the first 
president of the world government?

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.860
I'd think you'd do a 
surprisingly good job, Tohru.

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:18.490
You should dream more.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:21.240
No, that's a bit too much.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:24.280
Speaking of dreams...

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:28.120
I had a dream about a younger sister.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.370
You had a younger sister, Tohru?

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:33.000
I don't.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:35.670
But there was a girl
that felt like a younger sister...

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:37.670
...in that dream.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.510
I see... What kind of girl was she?

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.380
Let's see...

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.100
See that girl over there?

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:49.770
Someone like her...

00:12:57.360 --> 00:12:58.440
Sorry, give me a minute.

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.780
Jeez, you need to be more careful!

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.050
Tohru... look.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:31.930
HELP ME

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:33.640
Should we call security?

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:51.850
<b>KEEP OUT</b>

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.710
I hope she didn't come this way...

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:01.210
There we go.

00:14:15.350 --> 00:14:17.480
I had no idea this place existed...

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:01.440
Are you all right?

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:05.070
I'll be right over there.

00:15:06.110 --> 00:15:08.110
It's okay. Just stay put.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.420
<b>10 Big Topics Of 2015</b>

00:15:49.320 --> 00:15:49.820
Roger.

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.090
For real?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:14.220
This is insane!

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.450
Your life is mine to destroy!

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:40.000
Good going, Pug!

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:40.960
Next shot, fir—

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.380
Damn you!

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:54.890
If it's a fight you want,
it's a fight you get!

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:01.770
Let's make it showy!

00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:04.150
Ouch...

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.520
At this range?

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:09.190
Dammit!

00:17:28.380 --> 00:17:29.000
What's this?

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:47.230
Over here!

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:50.280
Tohru!

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:10.250
We fell down from up there, right?

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:12.590
I don't get this at all!

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:15.930
No reception. Figures.

00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:18.890
Seriously, where in the world are we?

00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.390
This building looks ancient.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:27.190
Tohru...

00:18:28.270 --> 00:18:29.520
That girl...

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:34.820
She disappeared.

00:18:38.910 --> 00:18:39.910
An earthquake?

00:18:40.330 --> 00:18:42.490
We should get downstairs quickly.

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.960
You're pretty calm.

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:48.170
You think so?

00:18:59.140 --> 00:19:01.350
A-Are you all right?

00:19:04.220 --> 00:19:05.350
Is he dead?

00:19:06.850 --> 00:19:08.230
He's been shot...

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:11.820
This floor. It's as if it...

00:19:17.150 --> 00:19:18.280
Another earthquake?

00:19:18.280 --> 00:19:20.410
No, that was an explosion!

00:19:20.410 --> 00:19:23.200
An explosion? What do you mean?

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:26.830
I don't know. In any case,
we should get out of here fast.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:27.540
Yeah.

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:30.580
We probably should have some weapons.

00:19:31.630 --> 00:19:32.540
Oh, no...

00:19:33.420 --> 00:19:34.300
This.

00:19:34.590 --> 00:19:36.970
Yeah. I should take one too.

00:19:47.640 --> 00:19:48.440
Damn you!

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:49.560
Let's go!

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.310
Yeah!

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:58.900
Kyoka!

00:20:00.320 --> 00:20:01.360
I'm fine...

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:03.030
It's nothing much.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:07.540
It'll be okay...

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.500
It's just like gym class.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.130
If that's the case,
I'm the best girl in my class!

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.550
We've got no choice!

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.360
This one is real!

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:22.450
I-I won't miss next time!

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:28.490
A bit late...

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:30.080
...aren't I?

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:39.750
You are...

00:21:40.260 --> 00:21:42.130
Tohru Kazasumi.

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:55.060
Open Hostilities: My Other Self

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:26.380
I'm Dogma.

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:27.200
I'm Magma.

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:29.450
We're the super mascots
that everyone's talking about!

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:31.450
We only have 15 seconds of screen time,
but everybody's talking about us?

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:35.250
Then, we'll get the ratings during the previews
and steal air time away from the main episode!

00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:37.080
Those eyes are serious.

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:40.040
<b><i>Resolve: </i></b>An Ending World<i><b></b></i>

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:38.860
Next episode: "Resolve"

00:23:38.860 --> 00:23:40.040
"An Ending World"
